{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cache-Control for Image Intermediaries.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cache-Control for Image Intermediaries.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cache control for image intermediaries cache control for image intermediaries","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cache-Control for Image Intermediaries.md","fileName":"Cache-Control for Image Intermediaries.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cache-Control for Image Intermediaries","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-28 04:01\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching","highperformanceimages.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cache-Control for Image Intermediaries.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cache-Control for Image Intermediaries.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cache control for image intermediaries cache control for image intermediaries","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cache-Control for Image Intermediaries.md","fileName":"Cache-Control for Image Intermediaries.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cache-Control for Image Intermediaries","heading":"Cache-Control for Image Intermediaries","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Image responses pass through browser caches, shared proxies, and CDNs that may not understand custom selection logic. Cache-Control determines whether those intermediaries may store a response, how long it remains fresh, and whether private data can be shared.\n\nA personalized or uncertain transformation may need private or no-transform directives, while stable public derivatives can be cached aggressively under versioned identities. Transport security helps prevent uncontrolled intermediaries from rewriting or confusing selected variants.","tags":